{"tool_name":"rnashapes","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"rnashapes","identifiers":["biotools:rnashapes","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btu649"],"license":"Not available","summary":"Rnashape abstraction maps structures to a tree-like domain of shapes, retaining adjacency and nesting of structural features, but disregarding helix lengths. Shape abstraction integrates well with dynamic programming algorithms, and hence it can be applied during structure prediction rather than afterwards. This avoids exponential explosion and can still give us a nonheuristic and complete account of properties of the molecules folding space.","home_url":"http://bibiserv.techfak.uni-bielefeld.de/rnashapes","keywords":["Computational Biology","Coronavirus","Nucleic Acid Conformation","RNA","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Structure prediction"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":52288},"biotools":{"id":"rnashapes","home":"http://bibiserv2.cebitec.uni-bielefeld.de/rnashapes","summary":"Integration of tools for RNA abstract shape analysis.","addition_date":"2017-12-18T00:11:54Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:19:38.590977Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["3.3.0"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:rnashapes","credit":[{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.techfak.uni-bielefeld.de/~sjanssen/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bibiserv2.cebitec.uni-bielefeld.de/rnashapes?id=rnashapes_rnashapes_manual_manual"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Prediction and recognition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2423"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Protein structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0474"}]}],"name":"RNAshapes","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btu649","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Abstract shape analysis, first proposed in 2004, allows one to extract several relevant structures from the folding space of an RNA sequence, preferable to focusing in a single structure of minimal free energy. We report recent extensions to this approach. Results: We have rebuilt the original RNAshapes as a repository of components that allows us to integrate several established tools for RNA structure analysis: RNAshapes, RNAalishapes and pknotsRG, including its recent extension pKiss. As a spin-off, we obtain heretofore unavailable functionality: e. g. with pKiss, we can now perform abstract shape analysis for structures holding pseudoknots up to the complexity of kissing hairpin motifs. The new tool pAliKiss can predict kissing hairpin motifs from aligned sequences. Along with the integration, the functionality of the tools was also extended in manifold ways.","authors":[{"name":"Giegerich R."},{"name":"Janssen S."}],"citationCount":101,"date":"2015-07-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"The RNA shapes studio"},"pmcid":"PMC4308662","pmid":"25273103","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0099"},{"term":"Structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0082"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"RNAshapes","home":"https://bio.tools/rnashapes","version":"3.3.0","summary":"Integration of tools for RNA abstract shape analysis.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:rnashapes:3.3.0/cmd/bibiserv2.cebitec.uni-bielefeld.de","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":78,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"-1"},{"count":4,"year":"2019"},{"count":4,"year":"2021"},{"count":4,"year":"2026"},{"count":5,"year":"2017"},{"count":6,"year":"2015"},{"count":6,"year":"2025"},{"count":7,"year":"2016"},{"count":7,"year":